{"name":"Bahia","hex":"#a9c01c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bahia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A state of the Northeast Region, Brazil. Capital: Salvador."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bahia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bahia","blocks":[{"text":"Bahia is one of the 26 states of Brazil, located in the Northeast Region of the country. It is the fourth-largest Brazilian state by population and the 5th-largest by area. Bahia's capital is the city of Salvador, on a spit of land separating the Bay of All Saints from the Atlantic. Once a stronghold of supporters of direct rule of Brazil by the Portuguese monarchy, and dominated by agricultural, slaving, and ranching interests, Bahia is now a predominantly working-class industrial and agricultural state. The state is home to 7% of the Brazilian population and produces 4.2% of the country's GDP. It is divided into 417 municipalities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Bandeira_da_Bahia.svg/330px-Bandeira_da_Bahia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahia","wikidata":"Q40430"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Global_Forest_Change_tree-cover_loss_year_in_Bahia%2C_2001-2024.png/500px-Global_Forest_Change_tree-cover_loss_year_in_Bahia%2C_2001-2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Global_Forest_Change_tree-cover_loss_year_in_Bahia%2C_2001-2024.png/500px-Global_Forest_Change_tree-cover_loss_year_in_Bahia%2C_2001-2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tree-cover loss year in Bahia, 2001-2024, from the Global Forest Change dataset.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlobal_Forest_Change_tree-cover_loss_year_in_Bahia%2C_2001-2024.png"},{"srcset":